From ba0c798b356173e2851dad35ad1f1986ca5de339 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:24:06 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] [UPSTREAM] notifications: harden sinks per review
 (redirects, secrets, concurrency)

Hardening of the notification sinks (0001-0004) after the Antigravity review:

- BLOCKING: the notification HTTP client now disables redirects
  (reqwest::redirect::Policy::none()). reqwest strips Authorization on a
  cross-origin 30x but NOT a custom credential header like X-Gotify-Key, so a
  redirecting proxy / captive portal could otherwise harvest the Gotify token.
  Credential header values are also marked sensitive.
- Empty-string secrets (ntfy_auth="" / gotify_token="") no longer send a blank
  header; a header value with invalid bytes is dropped rather than sent.
- gotify_url with a query/fragment is handled (insert /message before ?...).
- Webhook payload timestamp is the notification's receipt time, not the retry
  time after a backhaul outage (NotificationStatus.event_time).
- Sinks are delivered concurrently per tick (JoinSet), so a slow/hung sink no
  longer blocks delivery to the healthy ones (head-of-line blocking).
- test_notification works for a webhook-only or Gotify-only setup and applies
  ntfy_headers, using the same redirect-disabled client.
- Tests: send_notification strips the URL from a transport error; webhook
  payload has no subscriber-identifier fields; LowBattery/Update header and
  priority mappings; gotify_message_url slash/query handling.
- Nitpicks: sink_urls.get() (no panicking index); sink-collect comment includes
  Gotify; stale enabled_notifications config comment; resolve_endpoint_secret_*
  / redacts_secrets test names.

Ref: Orbic-Rayhunter T-OR-045..049 (PR #16 review follow-up).
Signed-off-by: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
